  "name": null,
  "problem": "Which of the following probabilities could be approximated using the normal approximation of the binomial distribution?\n\nI. The probability of finding more than $120$ people with blood type O+ in a randomly selected sample of $200$ if $53%$ of the population has blood type O+.\n\nII. The probability of finding less than $4$ defective items in a random sample of $100$ items produced by a machine if $2%$ of the items made are defective.\n\nIII. The probability that a biased coin lands on heads $9$ times out of $15$ coin flips if the probability of a single flip landing on heads is $0.25.$",
